From: YapLabs <folia@yaplabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] YaP force-partition along the carved corridor

Packed-spawn carve empties the hole then requestPartition recuts the
median. That ignores the gap, stays force-partition deferred, and never
logs "into 2 shards". After carve, split left/right of the pending plan.
If the corridor is still loaded, say so — do not recarve as if the cut
never happened. Empty-strip bar still carves first; this only changes
the retry after a finished carve. Goal: one live hot-region split.
Post-applyAllPatches.
---

--- a/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapSubRegionCuts.java
+++ b/folia-server/src/minecraft/java/io/papermc/paper/threadedregions/YapSubRegionCuts.java
@@ -102,6 +102,67 @@
         return out;
     }
 
     /**
+     * Split along an already-carved corridor. Median recut after a packed-spawn carve
+     * ignores the hole and stays {@code force-partition deferred}.
+     * Corridor sections (lo..hi) are omitted — they must already be empty.
+     */
+    static <R extends ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionData<R, S>, S extends ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSectionData>
+    List<List<ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S>>> cutAlongPlan(
+            final List<ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S>> sections,
+            final boolean cutOnX,
+            final int lo,
+            final int hi) {
+        final List<List<ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S>>> out = new ArrayList<>();
+        if (sections == null || sections.size() < 2 || lo > hi) {
+            return out;
+        }
+        final List<ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S>> left = new ArrayList<>();
+        final List<ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S>> right = new ArrayList<>();
+        int corridorLoaded = 0;
+        for (final ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S> s : sections) {
+            final int coord = cutOnX ? s.sectionX : s.sectionZ;
+            if (coord >= lo && coord <= hi) {
+                if (!s.isEmpty()) {
+                    corridorLoaded++;
+                } else {
+                    left.add(s);
+                }
+                continue;
+            }
+            if (coord < lo) {
+                left.add(s);
+            } else {
+                right.add(s);
+            }
+        }
+        if (corridorLoaded > 0 || left.isEmpty() || right.isEmpty()) {
+            return out;
+        }
+        out.add(left);
+        out.add(right);
+        return out;
+    }
+
+    static <R extends ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionData<R, S>, S extends ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSectionData>
+    int countCorridorLoaded(
+            final List<ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S>> sections,
+            final boolean cutOnX,
+            final int lo,
+            final int hi) {
+        int n = 0;
+        if (sections == null) {
+            return 0;
+        }
+        for (final ThreadedRegionizer.ThreadedRegionSection<R, S> s : sections) {
+            final int coord = cutOnX ? s.sectionX : s.sectionZ;
+            if (coord >= lo && coord <= hi && !s.isEmpty()) {
+                n++;
+            }
+        }
+        return n;
+    }
+
